GA "Genetic Algorithm" in its classic form (see page \pageref{secGA})
EDA "Estimation of Distribution Algorithm" a type of EA based on probabilistic models (page \pageref{algorithmEDA})
UMDA "Univariate Marginal Distribution Algorithm" a type of EDA (page \pageref{algorithmUMDA})
BMDA "Bivariate Marginal Distribution Algorithm" a type of EDA (page \pageref{algorithmBMDA})
BOA "Bayesian Optimization Algorithm" a type of EDA using Bayesian networks as the probabilistic model
EA "Evolutionary Algorithm" superclass of search algorithms mentioned in this work
VEGA "Vector Evaluated Genetic Algorithm" a simple multi-criteria GA (page \pageref{algorithmVEGA})
SPEA "Strength Pareto Evolutionary Algorithm" a multi-criteria GA with an elite containing clustered Pareto-optimal individuals (page \pageref{algorithmSPEA})
SAC "Strict Avalanche Criterion" see page \pageref{critSAC}
CGP "Cartesian Genetic Programming" see page \pageref{algorithmCGP}
DES "Data Encryption Standard" cipher with 56-bit key developed in the 1970s, no longer secure in its original form
AES "Advanced Encryption Standard" the Rijndael cipher approved as a standard
UML "Unified Modeling Language" a set of formalized graphical representations for program design/modeling
GaLib "Genetic Algorithm Library" library for genetic algorithms and genetic programming \cite{galib}
CREW "Concurrent Read Exclusive Write" one of the possible parallelism models
MOSAC "maximal order SAC" SAC of the highest possible order
RC4 "Rivest Cipher 4" one of the symmetric stream ciphers by Ron Rivest, who also co-developed RSA
MD5 "Message Digest 5" one of the hash algorithms by Ron Rivest, who also co-developed RSA
RSA "Rivest -- Shamir -- Adleman" the most famous asymmetric cipher, based on factorization of the product of two large prime numbers, the principle was invented earlier in Britain but kept secret, independently the same was discovered by the trio of Americans
DSA "Digital Signature Algorithm" digital signature algorithm based on discrete logarithms
SHA "Secure Hash Algorithm" standardized hash algorithm, currently SHA2, SHA3 in development
GP "Genetic Programming" evolutionary algorithm working directly with executable structures instead of numerical chromosomes
BF "Branching factor" (see subsection \ref{secBF} on page \pageref{secBF})
POSIX "Portable Operating System Interface" standardized portable interface for operating systems
GCC "Gnu Compiler Collection" a suite of compilers for various languages for UNIX systems \url{http://gcc.gnu.org/}
